<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Minangkabau people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Minangkabau are an Austronesian people of the highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-sumatra">West Sumatra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, known for their matrilineal society, in which land and houses pass through the female line. Their highlands were a source of gold for the ports of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-malacca">Strait of Malacca</a> and the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pagaruyung">Pagaruyung</a> kingdom. Many Minangkabau migrated, settling among other places in what became Negeri Sembilan in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/minangkabau-people.jpg" alt="Minangkabau people" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RahmatdenasMuffin Wizard This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape . · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Minang.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
